app ui-space-station-board "1.0.0"
"SpaceStationBoard — sci-fi isometric crew board: crew units select/move across a station grid (no combat); composes the std multi-unit crew frame with a hand-authored isometric svg asset theme."
;; @capabilities "isometric crew unit selection, station grid movement, multi-unit crew management, non-combat sci-fi sim"

;; ============================================================================
;; PERSONA + USER STORIES
;;
;; Read these before changing anything here, and walk them end to end after.
;; One persona: the PLAYER, directing a three-person station crew on a 7x7
;; isometric deck. Status verified 2026-07-31 through the almadar-tools
;; play_transition probes (guard truth, real evaluator) on the std-crew-board-2d
;; frame this organism composes; canvas-drawable claims verified at the
;; descriptor level. No claim below is untested hearsay.
;;
;; THE GENRE (what a station-crew-sim player expects): a calm, non-combat
;; sandbox. You run a small crew aboard a space station — there are no
;; enemies, no turns, no win/lose clock. The pleasure is directing people:
;; pick a crew member, see where they can walk (the deck is the constraint —
;; walls ring the station, console blocks are furniture you path around),
;; send them there, and watch the station live. A round looks like: click a
;; crew member -> green reachable floor cells light up (range 2, manhattan)
;; -> click a lit cell -> the crew member WALKS there (walk frames play)
;; -> the board settles back to idle, ready for the next order. Walls and
;; consoles are impassable; crew cannot stack on one cell. The HUD is station
;; chrome: Crew count, Oxygen, current Status. (Oxygen is display-only — the
;; organism never depletes it; that sim layer does not exist yet.)
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; PLAYER — "I direct my crew around the station deck."
;;
;;   1. I open the board and see the whole station deck framed on screen —
;;      a walled 7x7 isometric grid, floor inside, four console blocks, my
;;      three crew standing on the deck, and the HUD showing Crew/Oxygen/
;;      Status with a Cancel button and the minimap on.
;;        WORKS. Boot paints 49 full-cell isometric terrain cubes (wall ring
;;        impassable, floor interior, console blocks at (1,2),(5,2),(1,4),
;;        (5,4)), 3 crew units (Commander (2,3), Engineer (4,3), Technician
;;        (3,5)), 4 console features ground-anchored ON their cells, HUD
;;        reads Crew 3 / Oxygen 100 / Status idle.
;;   2. Every crew member is a visible sprite with a name label and a health
;;      bar I can read at a glance — and it breathes.
;;        WORKS. Each unit paints units/crew.svg url-rewritten to the
;;        .idle-<0..3> frames (4-frame breathing squash/stretch anchored at
;;        the feet, cycled by the AnimClock tick at ~300ms/frame), anchor
;;        "ground", with the black backing + green health fraction above and
;;        the name label. A hidden warm-up layer preloads every frame so
;;        state swaps never pop.
;;   3. I click a crew member and the cells they can reach light up green.
;;        WORKS. Clicking u1 sets phase "movement" and lights exactly the
;;        manhattan-2 diamond of PASSABLE floor cells minus occupied cells —
;;        walls and consoles never light up (guard + highlight filter both
;;        check passable). Clicking a unit already selected deselects it
;;        instead (toggle arm).
;;   4. I click a lit cell and the crew member walks there.
;;        WORKS. TILE_CLICK on an in-range, passable, unoccupied cell emits
;;        MOVE; the hero-nav authority re-checks bounds/budget and writes
;;        the position, the intent layer arms the walk animation (6 ticks of
;;        .walk-<0..1> frames), then selection/validMoves clear and phase
;;        returns to "idle". Verified by probe: (2,3) -> (3,3).
;;   5. I click a wall, a console, an occupied cell, or a cell beyond reach
;;      and nothing happens — the order is rejected, not silently eaten.
;;        WORKS. The TILE_CLICK arm's guard requires in-bounds AND
;;        manhattan <= movementRange AND unoccupied AND the target tile
;;        passable — all four probed: wall (0,0), console (1,2), occupied
;;        (4,3), out-of-range (6,6) all fail the guard. (Before the
;;        wave-3 fix the passable clause was missing in both the guard and
;;        the highlight filter — crew could walk onto walls/consoles.)
;;   6. I change my mind mid-order and back out cleanly.
;;        WORKS. CANCEL (button) clears selection, green cells, and phase;
;;        re-clicking the selected unit does the same via the toggle arm.
;;   7. I direct the whole crew, one order at a time — every member moves
;;      independently.
;;        WORKS. No per-turn activation locks (this is a sandbox, not a
;;        tactics game): after u1 walks, u2 selects and walks on the next
;;        order; moveBudget is effectively unlimited. Crew cannot be ordered
;;        onto each other's cells (occupied guard).
;;   8. The HUD reads like station chrome: crew count, oxygen, live status.
;;        WORKS. HUD shows Crew 3 and Oxygen 100 as numbers and the phase
;;        badge flips idle -> movement on selection and back on resolve.
;;        TRUTH: Oxygen and Crew are display-only (config seeds them at
;;        INIT; no atom writes them after) — documented on the molecule
;;        config, not a bug.
;;
;; ASSET INVENTORY (hand-authored svg, almadar-kflow-assets.web.app
;; /shared/ui-space-station-board/svg/isometric/, generated by
;; tools/asset-workflow svg-generator from the sibling .md descriptions)
;;
;;   Terrain   terrain/{wall,floor,console}.svg — full-cell isometric cubes
;;             (top + left + right faces) that tessellate exactly with the
;;             projector's cellPath; drawn at width/height 1, anchor center.
;;   Units     units/crew.svg + animation frames .{idle-0..3, walk-0..1,
;;             attack-0, hit-0, death-0}.svg (the full actor contract, though
;;             this non-combat board only ever plays idle/walk); the frame
;;             swaps url-rewrites name.svg -> name.<anim>-<i>.svg.
;;             crew: u1 Commander (2,3)  u2 Engineer (4,3)  u3 Technician (3,5)
;;   Features  features/console.svg at (1,2),(5,2),(1,4),(5,4) — drawn from
;;             config.features anchored "ground" at 1x1 so they sit ON their
;;             cells (the draw-sprite default anchor is "top-left", which
;;             floated them off the board corner before the anchor was
;;             explicit in the frame molecule).
;;   UI chrome ui/panel-frame.svg = game-shell background + HUD panel;
;;             ui/{icon-crew,icon-oxygen,icon-cancel}.svg = HUD stat/button
;;             icons.
;; ============================================================================

orbital SpaceStationBoardOrbital {
  uses Frame from "std/behaviors/std-crew-board-2d"

  type Asset = {
    url : asset
    atlas : asset
    sprite : string
    role : string
    category : string
    animations : [string]
    style : string
    dimension : string
    aspect : string
    name : string
    thumbnailUrl : string
  }
  type Unit = {
    id : string!
    position : { x : number!  y : number! }
    x : number
    y : number
    z : number
    team : string
    health : number
    maxHealth : number
    unitType : string
    name : string
    modelUrl : Asset
  }
  type Tile = {
    id : string
    x : number!
    y : number!
    z : number
    terrain : string
    passable : boolean
    terrainSprite : Asset
  }
  type Fx = {
    id : string!
    type : string!
    x : number!
    z : number
    y : number
    message : string
    ttl : number!
  }
  type ValidMove = { x : number!  z : number! }
  type Feature = {
    id : string
    x : number!
    y : number!
    z : number
    type : string
    assetUrl : Asset
    color : string
    elevation : number
  }
  type AssetManifest = {
    terrains : Map string Asset
    units : Map string Asset
    features : Map string Asset
    effects : Map string Asset
  }

  entity GameState [runtime, shared] {
    id : string!
    units : [Unit] = []
    tiles : [Tile] = []
    movesLeft : number = 0
    fx : [Fx] = []
    selectedUnitId : string = ""
    validMoves : [ValidMove] = []
    phase : string = "idle"
    oxygen : number = 100
    crewCount : number = 3
  }

  trait CrewAuthority = Frame.traits.CrewAuthority -> GameState {
    config {
      running: true
      gridWidth: 7
      gridHeight: 7
      moveBudget: 999999
      units: [
        { id: "u1", position: { x: 2, y: 3 }, x: 2, y: 3, z: 0, team: "player", health: 10, maxHealth: 10, unitType: "crew", name: "Commander", modelUrl: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.json", sprite: "robot_blue.png", role: "npc", category: "crew", animations: ["idle","walk","attack","hit","death"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "crew", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "u2", position: { x: 4, y: 3 }, x: 4, y: 3, z: 0, team: "player", health: 10, maxHealth: 10, unitType: "crew", name: "Engineer", modelUrl: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.json", sprite: "robot_blue.png", role: "npc", category: "crew", animations: ["idle","walk","attack","hit","death"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "crew", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "u3", position: { x: 3, y: 5 }, x: 3, y: 5, z: 0, team: "player", health: 10, maxHealth: 10, unitType: "crew", name: "Technician", modelUrl: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-robot-pack/units/spritesheet_robotsTop.json", sprite: "robot_blue.png", role: "npc", category: "crew", animations: ["idle","walk","attack","hit","death"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "crew", thumbnailUrl: "" } }
      ]
      tiles: [
        { id: "t-0-0", x: 0, y: 0, terrain: "wall", passable: false, terrainSprite: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.json", sprite: "abstractTile_01.png", role: "tile", category: "wall", animations: ["static"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "wall", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "t-1-0", x: 1, y: 0, terrain: "wall", passable: false, terrainSprite: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.json", sprite: "abstractTile_01.png", role: "tile", category: "wall", animations: ["static"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "wall", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "t-2-0", x: 2, y: 0, terrain: "wall", passable: false, terrainSprite: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.json", sprite: "abstractTile_01.png", role: "tile", category: "wall", animations: ["static"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "wall", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "t-3-0", x: 3, y: 0, terrain: "wall", passable: false, terrainSprite: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.json", sprite: "abstractTile_01.png", role: "tile", category: "wall", animations: ["static"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "wall", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
        { id: "t-4-0", x: 4, y: 0, terrain: "wall", passable: false, terrainSprite: { url: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.png", atlas: "https://almadar-kflow-assets.web.app/shared/ui-space-station-board/kenney-isometric-blocks/terrain/allTiles_sheet.json", sprite: "abstractTile_01.png", role: "tile", category: "wall", animations: ["static"], style: "sci-fi", dimension: "2d", aspect: "1:1", name: "wall", thumbnailUrl: "" } },
